  FORMAT:  admit <ID> <age> <stage> [flags] [mental] [mins]

  ── REQUIRED FIELDS ─────────────────────────────────────

  ID      Patient identifier. Any text, no spaces.
          e.g.  PT-042  or  JOHN  or  BED-7

  age     Patient age in years (1–120).
          Children under 16 and seniors 65+ are flagged
          automatically — they have a 15hr timeline vs 24hr.

  stage   Infection stage 1–6.
          1  Early onset — fully curable
          2  Mild symptoms — fully curable
          3  Moderate — fully curable
          4  Advanced — reduced cure chance
             NOTE: Stage 2 with throat flag (T) is reclassified
             as Stage 4 automatically.
          5  Critical — last resort vaccine only
          6  Terminal — euthanasia if past 10-min window

  ── OPTIONAL FLAGS (add in any order after stage) ────────

  E       Essential personnel.
          Doctors, nurses, soldiers, security.
          Loss of essential staff multiplies casualties.

  H       Hot environment / high body mass.
          Accelerates zombification — increases urgency.

  T       Throat tightness / breathing difficulty.
          Indicates possible Stage 2 → Stage 4 misread.
          System will reclassify automatically if Stage 2.

  S       Sterile environment (hospital / clean home).
          Reduces spread risk — slightly lowers urgency.

  ── MENTAL HEALTH STATE (0–4, default = 0) ───────────────

  More negative mental state = faster virus spread.
  Enter a single digit after any flags.

  0   Stable     — no effect on spread
  1   Anxious    — mild acceleration (x1.25)
  2   Depressed  — moderate acceleration (x1.50)
  3   Severe     — strong acceleration (x1.75)
                   bumps curable patients to Tier 2
  4   Crisis     — maximum acceleration (x2.00)
                   treat immediately before state worsens

  ── MINUTES TO TRANSFORMATION (stage 5/6 only) ───────────

  Enter estimated minutes remaining before full zombification.
  Only relevant for Stage 5 and Stage 6 patients.

  Stage 6 decision logic:
    <= 10 min  →  VACCINATE (emergency last resort)
